#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:9
msgid "Using crack submodels in PyBaMM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:11
msgid ""
"In this notebook we show how to use the crack submodel with battery DFN or "
"SPM models. To see all of the models and submodels available in PyBaMM, "
"please take a look at the documentation `here <https://docs.pybamm.org/en/"
"latest/source/api/models/index.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:-1
msgid "[1]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"%pip install \"pybamm[plot,cite]\" -q    # install PyBaMM if it is not "
"installed\n"
"import os\n"
"\n"
"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n"
"\n"
"import pybamm\n"
"\n"
"os.chdir(pybamm.__path__[0] + \"/..\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:39
msgid ""
"Then we load the DFN, SPMe or SPM, by choosing one and commenting the others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:41
msgid ""
"When you load a model in PyBaMM it builds by default. Building the model "
"sets all of the model variables and sets up any variables which are coupled "
"between different submodels: this is the process which couples the submodels "
"together and allows one submodel to access variables from another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:-1
msgid "[2]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"model = pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN(\n"
"    options={\n"
"        \"particle\": \"Fickian diffusion\",\n"
"        \"particle mechanics\": \"swelling and cracking\",  # other options "
"are \"none\", \"swelling only\"\n"
"    }\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:67
msgid ""
"Load the parameter set Ai2020 which contains mechanical parameters. Other "
"sets may not contain mechanical parameters should add them manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:-1
msgid "[3]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"param = pybamm.ParameterValues(\"Ai2020\")\n"
"## It can update the speed of crack propagation using the commands below:\n"
"# param.update({\"Negative electrode Cracking rate\":3.9e-20*10}, )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:90
msgid ""
"We can get the default parameters for the model and update them with the "
"parameters required by the cracking model. Eventually, we would like these "
"to be added to their own chemistry (you might need to adjust the path to the "
"parameters file to your system). Now the model can be processed and solved "
"in the usual way, and we still have access to model defaults such as the "
"default geometry and default spatial methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:101
msgid ""
"Depending on the parameter set being used, the particle cracking model can "
"require a large number of mesh points inside the particles to be numerically "
"stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:-1
msgid "[4]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"var_pts = {\n"
"    \"x_n\": 20,  # negative electrode\n"
"    \"x_s\": 20,  # separator\n"
"    \"x_p\": 20,  # positive electrode\n"
"    \"r_n\": 26,  # negative particle\n"
"    \"r_p\": 26,  # positive particle\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:-1
msgid "[5]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"sim = pybamm.Simulation(\n"
"    model,\n"
"    parameter_values=param,\n"
"    var_pts=var_pts,\n"
")\n"
"solution = sim.solve(t_eval=[0, 3600], inputs={\"C-rate\": 1})\n"
"# plot\n"
"quick_plot = pybamm.QuickPlot(solution)\n"
"quick_plot.dynamic_plot()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/submodel_cracking_DFN_or_SPM.ipynb:147
msgid ""
